y is checked every 1 day, with holding cost at $3.172 per unit and shortage cost at $33.297 per unit. SoC is also reviewed every 1 day, and shortages cost $45.694 per unit. Finished goods move from the Integration Center to the Logistics Center for distribution. On the demand side, Schneider Electric buys FPGA, placing orders with exponentially distributed interarrival times averaging 53 days. Each order requests between 982547 units and 4624082 units, delivery is promised in exactly 15 days, and the selling price is $3016.709 per unit. If stock is short, available units ship right away and the balance is backordered, and customer payment comes in exactly 38 days. ABB Industrial purchases SoC on a steady 27-day cycle, with order sizes ranging from 2048293 units to 2225946 units. Their delivery lead time is exactly 2 days, the sales price is $1176.502 per unit, and any unmet portion is backordered after immediate partial shipment; payment is received between 15 days and 61 days later. The model runs for a 500-day horizon, with results collected after a 30-day warm-up period, and 1 replication is used.

