This setup centers on producing the SoC for ABB Industrial, with the network linking ElectroParts, FastChip Corp., and PrecisionParts to Advanced Fab and then on to the Fulfillment Hub. The finished SoC is built from 1 cooling_unit, 1 silicon_wafer, 1 lithium_cell, and 1 aluminum_sheet, while each cooling_unit itself is made from 4 units of lithium_cell, 2 units of aluminum_sheet, and 2 units of silicon_wafer. At the raw material level, aluminum_sheet, lithium_cell, and silicon_wafer are all sourced on an as-needed basis. Aluminum_sheet inventory is reviewed every 27 hours and carries a holding cost of $6.509 per unit, while silicon_wafer is reviewed every 3 hours with a shortage cost of $1.346 per unit. ElectroParts supplies aluminum_sheet with a fixed 19.0-hour lead time, charges $123.343 per unit, offers payment due 24.0 days after delivery, and can supply up to 733160 units per order; shipping from ElectroParts to Advanced Fab takes between 2.0 and 8.0 hours. FastChip Corp. provides lithium_cell with an exponentially distributed lead time averaging 29.0 hours, a unit cost of $216.042, net 54.0-day payment terms, and a maximum order size of 443571 units; transfer to Advanced Fab takes exactly 4.0 hours. PrecisionParts handles silicon_wafer with a consistent 17.0-hour lead time, a price of $373.373 per unit, payment terms ranging from 49.0 to 83.0 days, and capacity capped at 71334 units. Advanced Fab manages aluminum_sheet, cooling_unit, silicon_wafer, lithium_cell, and SoC inventory, and it starts with 3479849 units of cooling_unit and 3718799 units of SoC on hand. The plant’s cutting operation turns cooling_unit, silicon_wafer, lithium_cell, and aluminum_sheet into SoC, with each run taking anywhere from 9.0 to 23.0 hours. A Quality Scanner supports the process with capacity for 1 unit at a time, an exponentially distributed service time with a mean of 1.809 hours, and an operating cost of $17.275 per hour. On the demand side, ABB Industrial places orders for SoC every 48.0 hours, with demand centered around 4832729.0 units and varying by about 806361.0 units. Customer deliveries take exactly 25.0 hours, the selling price is $2664.426 per unit, and customer payments arrive between 11.0 and 50.0 days later. If stock runs short, available units are shipped and the remaining demand is lost, and the SoC inventory is reviewed every 1 hour with a shortage cost of $49.04 per unit. The model runs for 365 hours total, with the first 30 hours treated as warm-up, and includes 10 replications.

