s key step is polishing, where carbon_fiber, memory_chip, gold_wire, and sensor_array are consumed to produce industrial_sensor, and that cycle runs in a uniform 9.0-day to 16.0-day range. The site also has a Laser Cutter with capacity for 1 unit at a time; its processing time ranges from 2.205 days to 8.076 days, and it costs $8.322 per day to operate. On the demand side, Ross Associates buys industrial_sensor units, placing orders at intervals between 13.0 days and 38.0 days. Order volume is centered around 3230586.0 units, varying by about 538595.0 units, and customer deliveries take between 14.0 days and 23.0 days. If stock runs short, available units are shipped immediately and the remaining demand is backordered. The selling price is $2250.294 per unit, and Ross Associates pays exactly 39.0 days after delivery. Structurally, all 3 suppliers connect into the Assembly Hub, and finished industrial_sensor units flow from the Assembly Hub to the Distribution Center. The model runs in days over a 730-day horizon with 10 replications.

