th 1205614 units, with a holding cost of $6.561 per unit, a shortage cost of $22.681 per unit, and a 1 day review cycle. EV_battery opens with 3783465 units, carries $5.759 per unit in holding cost, $38.742 per unit in shortage cost, and is also reviewed every 1 day. Demand comes from three major customers. Dell Technologies buys FPGA, placing orders every 48.0 days, with demand typically around 1475227.0 units and variability of 181293.0 units; delivery is expected between 8.0 days and 16.0 days, available units ship immediately and the remainder is backordered, the selling price is $2149.422 per unit, and payment arrives 17.0 days later. HP Enterprise purchases EV_battery with order arrivals averaging 28.0 days, demand centered on 2428218.0 units with variation of 621199.0 units, and customer lead times ranging from 9.0 days to 22.0 days; under short supply, whatever inventory is available is shipped and the rest is lost, the price is $3799.883 per unit, and payment is received after 58.0 days. Sony Electronics is another FPGA customer, with requests arriving on average every 42.0 days, demand roughly 3147385.0 units with variability of 367045.0 units, a fixed 16.0 days delivery expectation, and the same partial-fill, lost-remainder approach when stock is short; Sony pays $2252.024 per unit, with remittance coming between 17.0 days and 62.0 days. The full setup is evaluated over a 730 day horizon, with 10 replications.

